// What a government is trying to do, placed on two axes rather than listed as a set of
// mutually hostile boxes.
//
//     economic    -1 the state decides what is made  ·  +1 the market decides
//     authority   -1 the person is left alone        ·  +1 the state's word is final
//
// Everything diplomatic that depends on ideology is built from the distance between two
// positions. That is why it is a position and not a table: a table of opinions between
// fifteen ideologies is two hundred and ten numbers nobody will keep in step, and a mod that
// adds a sixteenth would have to write thirty more. Place an ideology and every other
// ideology's opinion of it exists the moment it is placed.
//
// `prefers_governments` is where this ideology sits comfortably. Being outside the list is
// not forbidden - a liberal absolute monarchy is a thing that has happened - it costs
// `mismatch_stability` every week, which is the honest way to say "this is an unstable
// arrangement" rather than "this is not allowed".
//
// `effects` are weekly, except `growth`, which is annual.
//
// The first entry is what a country believes when nothing has said otherwise.

